{"title":"Career Roadmap — AUTOSAR Developer","role":"AUTOSAR Developer","summary":"An AUTOSAR Developer develops automotive embedded software using the AUTOSAR (AUTomotive Open System ARchitecture) standard. The role focuses on building standardized, modular and reusable software for Electronic Control Units (ECUs).","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Automotive Electronics / Autonomous Vehicles"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An AUTOSAR Developer develops automotive embedded software using the AUTOSAR (AUTomotive Open System ARchitecture) standard. The role focuses on building standardized, modular and reusable software for Electronic Control Units (ECUs)."},{"type":"p","text":"AUTOSAR development sits at the intersection of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Embedded C/C++"},{"text":"Automotive electronics"},{"text":"Real-time operating systems"},{"text":"Microcontrollers"},{"text":"CAN/LIN/FlexRay/Ethernet"},{"text":"AUTOSAR Classic/Adaptive"},{"text":"Diagnostics"},{"text":"Functional safety"},{"text":"Cybersecurity"},{"text":"Automotive software architecture"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Typical work includes developing AUTOSAR Basic Software, application software, RTE configurations, ECU abstraction layers, communication stacks and diagnostics functionality."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"Embedded C, microcontrollers, automotive protocols and AUTOSAR fundamentals"}],[{"text":"2030–2035"},{"text":"AUTOSAR Classic development, ECU integration, diagnostics and functional safety"}],[{"text":"2035–2040"},{"text":"AUTOSAR Adaptive, automotive Ethernet, zonal architectures and software-defined vehicles"}],[{"text":"2040–2046"},{"text":"Automotive Software Architect, AUTOSAR Architect, Principal Engineer or Vehicle Software Lead"}]]}]},{"heading":