:"ARM"},{"type":"p","text":"RTOS"},{"type":"p","text":"Interrupts"},{"type":"p","text":"Drivers"},{"type":"p","text":"Memory"},{"type":"p","text":"Debugging"},{"type":"h","text":"Automotive"},{"type":"p","text":"CAN"},{"type":"p","text":"CAN FD"},{"type":"p","text":"LIN"},{"type":"p","text":"Automotive Ethernet"},{"type":"p","text":"UDS"},{"type":"p","text":"DoIP"},{"type":"p","text":"SOME/IP"},{"type":"h","text":"AUTOSAR"},{"type":"p","text":"AUTOSAR Classic"},{"type":"p","text":"BSW"},{"type":"p","text":"MCAL"},{"type":"p","text":"RTE"},{"type":"p","text":"SWC"},{"type":"p","text":"ARXML"},{"type":"p","text":"ECU Configuration"},{"type":"p","text":"AUTOSAR Adaptive"},{"type":"h","text":"Safety & Security"},{"type":"p","text":"ISO 26262"},{"type":"p","text":"Functional Safety"},{"type":"p","text":"ISO/SAE 21434"},{"type":"p","text":"Automotive Cybersecurity"},{"type":"p","text":"Secure Boot"},{"type":"p","text":"OTA Security"},{"type":"h","text":"Tools"},{"type":"p","text":"CANoe"},{"type":"p","text":"CANalyzer"},{"type":"p","text":"DaVinci"},{"type":"p","text":"EB tresos"},{"type":"p","text":"TRACE32"},{"type":"p","text":"Git"},{"type":"p","text":"Jenkins"},{"type":"p","text":"CMake"}]},{"heading":"Target Profile by Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A strong graduate should be able to understand the complete path:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Vehicle Requirement","System Architecture","ECU / Software Component","AUTOSAR Configuration","RTE","BSW","MCAL","Microcontroller","CAN / Ethernet","ECU Integration","SIL / HIL Testing","Vehicle Validation"]},{"type":"flow","items":["They should also be capable of debugging issues across application software","RTE","BSW","communication stack","MCU/hardware"]}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For B.Tech/B.E. — Automotive Electronics / Autonomous Vehicles, AUTOSAR is a strong specialization, particularly for students interested in embedded automotive software."},{"type":"p","text":"The best positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Embedded C Developer","Automotive Communication Engineer","AUTOSAR Specialist"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest graduate profile is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Embedded C","Microcontrollers","RTOS","CAN/UDS","AUTOSAR Classic","AUTOSAR Adaptive","Automotive Ethernet","Functional Safety","Cybersecurity."],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"For the 2026+ automotive market, don't stop at AUTOSAR Classic. Build a progression toward AUTOSAR Adaptive + Linux/C++ + Automotive Ethernet + Software-Defined Vehicles, because those skills connect traditional ECU development with newer centralized and autonomous vehicle architectures."}]}]}